  "description": "SAXJAD crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C128 H144 Ce8 O10 Se18,5.25(C4 H8 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 1 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 2 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 2 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 2 O neighbors; Ce1B (Ce) has 1 O neighbors; Ce2B (Ce) has 2 O neighbors; Ce3B (Ce) has 2 O neighbors; Ce4B (Ce) has 2 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 4 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.877-3.956 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 117.08-124.47°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C128H144O10Ce8Se18·5.25(C4H8O).",
